        "rationale": "The requirement is structural. It says every criterion type implements `trust_but_verify::graph::Criterion<D>` for its application domain, and it gives the trait's shape: the `Send + Sized` bound, `Ok: Serialize + DeserializeOwned + Send`, the three identity methods, and an `execute` that returns a `Send` future. It has no separate observable behavioral obligation, so the tests only need to show that implementers can use that shape.\n\nThe marked tests do this:\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested]` uses the test criterion `impl[Review<O>/Criterion<Application>]` through `Validator` calls. It checks `source_node_id`, `criterion_path` and `version` on the resulting evidence, and it checks that the `Ok` values round-trip through serde storage.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[validation_and_answer_need_send_without_sync]` uses an `Ok` type that is `Send` but not `Sync`, so the trait cannot require `Sync` on `Ok`. It drives `verify`, `store_evidence`, `load_evidence` and `refresh_evidence` through a `send(...)` helper that needs `Send` futures. It also exercises the version-compatibility check and the identity members.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[caller_reuses_negative_answers_and_compares_revisions_explicitly]` and `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs#fn[deterministic_validation_uses_required_storage_without_an_agent]` implement and run further criteria. They exercise `version`, `source_node_id` and the deterministic `execute` path against different domains.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]` checks that the public export inventory matches the spec, and that the shipping Habeas consumer compiles against the SDK.\n\nA wrong trait shape would be caught at compile time by these implementations and uses. For example, a missing `Send` bound on the `execute` future, or an extra `Sync` bound on `Ok`, would break the `Cell` test. I found no other obligation that needs test evidence, and I found no missing test marker."
